  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilience to Wildfires and Extreme Heat through Innovative Early Warning and Community-Based Solutions in Mozambique and Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen resilience to wildfires by piloting innovative, community-led early warning systems (EWS) that integrate artificial intelligence (AI), sensor networks, and real-time data analytics including through Open Weather APIs. It also promotes nature-based mitigation strategies, such as reforestation and fire-resistant landscapes, and supports sustainable land-use planning through the Landscape-Integrated Knowledge Systems (LINKS) approach.</narrative>
  </description>
